tared:
imp. & p. p. of Tare
a. Weighed; determined; reduced to equal or standard weight;
   as, tared filter papers, used in weighing precipitates.

throats:
n. the passage to the stomach and lungs; in the front part of the neck below the chin and above the collarbone
n. an opening in the vamp of a shoe at the instep
n. a passage resembling a throat in shape or function;

triumphing:
p. pr. & vb. n. of Triumph
a. Having or celebrating a triumph; victorious;
   triumphant.
